{"total_count":3,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14328","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14328/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14328/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14328/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14328","id":6581147061,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABRiIUOQ","number":14328,"title":"id/web: guard /ws/tags broadcast frames at the boundary (#7983 item 2)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-24T11:53:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T11:57:32Z","closed_at":"2026-11-24T11:53:29Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/14328","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14328","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14328.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/14328.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-24T11:53:29Z"},"body":"## #7983 item 2 — pkgs/id/web response-cast inventory: last unguarded cast guarded\n\nRefs #14010 (item 2 of the #7983 remainder; items 3–10 follow as separate packets). Refs #7983.\n\n### The change\n\nThe `/ws/tags` broadcast handler in `pkgs/id/web/src/main.ts` parsed frames with `JSON.parse(event.data as string)` and read fields off the result with no shape check — the last unguarded response cast in the surface. It now routes through a new `parseTagWsEvent` guard in `tags-response.ts` (the module that already hosts `parseTagsResponse`): non-string frames are dropped, and a parsed frame must be a non-array object with a string `type` tag and string-or-null `subject`/`key`/`value`, or it is ignored — never refreshed against.\n\nTests: `tags-response.test.ts` gains the `parseTagWsEvent` control + fail-closed suites (28 tests in the file, all passing). Oracle: the TagEvent wire format in `book/reference/websockets.md`.\n\n### Inventory (every response site in the three named files, re-derived from source)\n\n- `main.ts` — `/api/identity/me` → `parseIdentityMeResponse`; identity register → `parseIdentityRegisterResponse`; identity name → `parseIdentityNameResponse`; `/api/tags` → `parseTagsResponse`; `/api/files/send` → `isSendFileResponse`; `/api/save` → `isSaveFileResponse`; `/api/new` → `isNewFileResponse`; `/api/rename` → `isRenameFileResponse`; `/api/copy` → `isCopyFileResponse`; `/ws/tags` frames → **guarded by this PR**. All other `as` casts in the file are DOM element typing, not response casts.\n- `world.ts` — host view → `parseWorldHostViewPage`; invite → `parseWorldInviteResponse`; the three `JSON.parse(...) as unknown` frame sites each check `isRecord` + string `type` before the `as WorldFrame` narrowing, with per-type deep guards (`isWorldSnapshot`, `isWorldEvent`, `hasNonStringField`) before fields are relied on.\n- `home.ts` — feed → `parseHomeFeed`.\n\nSo every cast either sits behind a boundary shape check in the surface error vocabulary, or is a narrowing behind one. No non-boundary dispositions were needed; the full item-2 record is posted on #7983.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `vitest run src/tags-response.test.ts` on this branch: 28/28 pass.\n- Implementing lane's checkpoint record: full web suite 46 files / 936 tests pass, `tsc` clean, biome clean.\n\n---\n\nCloses #14010\n\n(Linkage note, added post-merge for queue verification: this PR lands item 2 only. #14010 remains the open tracker for items 3–10 of the #7983 remainder — the keyword above records the PR↔issue closing reference and, the PR being already merged, does not close the issue.)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14328/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/14328/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11197","id":6442076589,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABPyqpBg","number":11197,"title":"Fix #7983 item 1: sync-models validates the language-server catalog shape","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12834279439,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAAC_PuQDw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/status/in-progress","name":"status/in-progress","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Queue worker lifecycle state","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12834737120,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAAC_QKL4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/work/assigned","name":"work/assigned","color":"FEF2C0","default":false,"description":"Queue worker lifecycle state","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":13198401025,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-eAQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:gap-filed","name":"audit:gap-filed","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"Gap/next-step filed as new issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-17T10:02:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T02:17:00Z","closed_at":"2026-11-17T21:37:19Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/11197","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11197","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11197.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11197.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-17T21:37:19Z"},"body":"Closes item 1 of #7983 (parse-boundary shape checks, #3068 contract).\n\n## Change\n- `bin/sync-models.mjs`: the language-server `GetAvailableModels` response was read as `(await res.json()).response?.models || {}`, so shape drift read as zero models. It now goes through `parseLiveCatalogBody`, which requires a plain object body, a plain-object `response`, and a plain-object `response.models`. Any other shape throws a named `LiveCatalogShapeError` that is rethrown past the per-port probe loop instead of being swallowed. Malformed JSON (a syntax failure) keeps the existing per-port skip.\n- `bin/sync-models.test.mjs`: probe matrix (null, array, scalar, `{}`, wrong-typed `response` and `response.models`) plus a well-formed case.\n\n## Note on the site\nThe issue text places the site at the models.dev read (`:127`). The quoted expression `.response?.models || {}` is the language-server read at `:137` in this tree. This PR fixes that expression. The models.dev read at `:87` (`fetchModelsDev`, returns the parsed body unchecked) is not changed here; it is left for a follow-up item if the chain needs it.\n\n## Tests\n- `node --test bin/sync-models.test.mjs` — 55 pass, 0 fail.\n- `node --check bin/sync-models.mjs` — OK.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797501777&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11197&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11197&signature=ea680921540a9bd8897dd3e938c29471816ccc4d3b315fb35cd20d87509be644\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-ass